  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 139 PM CDT Sat Oct 17 2026\n\nTo what should be no surprise given trends this summer, our weekend \nspell of cooler fall weather will be short lived as the region will \nonce again see temperatures shoot up over the coming week as upper \nheights climb above 585 with the return of the southern upper ridge. \nThe NBM models depict a 25-75 percentile spread of only a few \ndegrees apart leading to high confidence in this warming trend.\n\nOf equal note is that the dry Canadian continental air mass has\nadvected all the way into the Gulf so even with the return flow\nthis week the pattern will keep the vertical pattern dry \nleading to a extremely low chance for any rainfall minimizing \nany recent improvements to the drought gained by last weeks \nrainfall. \n\nAs had been previously introduced, there remains at least medium\nconfidence in above normal temperatures to end October as the \nCPC has our entire region in a 60-70% chance for above normal \ntemperatures for the period of October 24-30.",
